    {
      "id": 1,
      "type": "Note",
      "pos": [
        40,
        -43.215850929109585
      ],
      "size": [
        490,
        400
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 1,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "OPTION B - UPSCALE THE PANORAMAS, THEN BUILD THE DATASET (best quality)\n\nUSE THIS when your SphereSfM node ran in mode=panorama_only, so the dataset folder\nholds raw equirect panoramas/ and NO SfM has run yet.\n\nWHY: the raw WAN equirect frames are already a perfectly coherent video, so SeedVR2\nupscales them with zero view-direction seams. Running SphereSfM on the UPSCALED\npanoramas also finds more/denser features -> better poses + cloud + sharp cube faces.\n\nFLOW\n1. Resolve Dataset Images reads the panorama_pending marker -> panoramas/ folder.\n2. Load Images (Path) reads the equirect frames (coherent video).\n3. SeedVR2 upscales them.\n4a. Save Upscaled Dataset preserves originals (panoramas_lowres/) + writes upscaled\n    panoramas back (safe, idempotent, re-run friendly).\n4b. SphereSfM Dataset (mode=colmap_now) runs SfM on the UPSCALED frames and writes\n    the final images/ + sparse/0/ COLMAP dataset into the SAME folder.\n\nHOW TO USE\n- Set 'dataset_name' on Resolve AND 'output_name' on the SphereSfM node to the SAME\n  name (the one you used when generating with mode=panorama_only).\n- Keep the SphereSfM SfM knobs matching what you intended at generation (the marker\n  recorded your choices for reference).\n- Keep 'lowres_suffix' identical on Resolve and Save.\n\nBATCH SIZE (important): batch_size is preset to 81 so each 81-frame path upscales as\none coherent clip (no cross-path bleed, no ragged batch). The Resolve node also PRINTS\na 'suggested_batch_size' to the console (largest 4n+1 divisor of your per-path frame\ncount) -- if your WAN length isn't 81, set batch_size to that printed value. OOM? drop\nto the next 4n+1 divisor (81 -> 9), or lower resolution / enable VAE tiling / DiT\noffload. uniform_batch_size is ON as a safety net.\n\nSeedVR2: 'resolution' = target shortest edge. Low VRAM -> lower batch_size + resolution,\nDiT loader offload_device=cpu + blocks_to_swap, VAE tiling."
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
